1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,231
Today is November 12, 2026.

3
00:00:07,231 --> 00:00:14,670
Overnight, the S and P, Nasdaq, and Dow surged during a Treasury holiday despite hawkish Fed warnings.

4
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:23,260
The S and P 500 rose 98 points, or 1.31 percent, closing at 7,619.

5
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:30,785
The Nasdaq jumped 400 points, or 1.6 percent, reclaiming its 250-day moving average.

6
00:00:30,785 --> 00:00:38,910
The Dow Jones added 255 points, or 0.49 percent, marking four straight positive sessions.

7
00:00:38,910 --> 00:00:46,704
The Philadelphia Semiconductor Index, ticker S-O-X, also vaulted back above its 250-day moving average.

8
00:00:46,704 --> 00:00:52,880
This rally repaired last week's panic over Democratic congressional wins slowing data center permits.

9
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:58,113
Positioning data reveals a classic institutional trap at last week's market bottom.

10
00:00:58,113 --> 00:01:04,498
Bank of America reports institutions bought 6.1 billion dollars of equities during the selloff.

11
00:01:04,498 --> 00:01:09,008
Hedge funds also turned net buyers for the first time in four weeks.

12
00:01:09,008 --> 00:01:16,177
Meanwhile, panicked retail investors capitulated, dumping 2.1 billion dollars in individual stocks.

13
00:01:16,177 --> 00:01:21,606
Crowded short positioning in the Q-Q-Q collided with a Negative Gamma options regime.

14
00:01:21,606 --> 00:01:27,746
The VIX plunged over 38 percent in four days, fueling massive mechanical short covering.

15
00:01:27,746 --> 00:01:34,241
Wednesday's Veterans Day holiday closed the Treasury market, temporarily removing bond yield pressure.

16
00:01:34,241 --> 00:01:39,927
However, dangerous divergences are emerging beneath the surface of this low-volume bounce.

17
00:01:39,927 --> 00:01:46,875
Treasury trading resumes today, forcing equities to digest hot inflation data and hawkish Fed remarks.

18
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:53,248
Chicago Fed President Austan Goolsbee warned that broad service inflation is overheating the economy.

19
00:01:53,248 --> 00:02:00,638
Philadelphia Fed President Anna Paulson, a 2026 voting member, stated further rate hikes are appropriate.

20
00:02:00,638 --> 00:02:07,562
Meanwhile, Abu Dhabi peace talks and Iran nuclear headlines remain mere geopolitical smokescreens.

21
00:02:07,562 --> 00:02:14,584
In Washington, tech giants now rely on President Trump's veto power against Democratic AI regulations.

22
00:02:14,584 --> 00:02:21,557
Technically, major indices now face heavy overhead resistance alongside glaring volume-price divergence.

23
00:02:21,557 --> 00:02:28,787
The S and P 500 must clear 7,715 and its descending channel to confirm a breakout.

24
00:02:28,787 --> 00:02:42,255
The Nasdaq 100 faces dual resistance at 29,000, matching 700 dollars on the Q-Q-Q. Closing at 695 dollars yesterday, the Q-Q-Q sits just below that 700 dollar ceiling.

25
00:02:42,255 --> 00:02:48,983
If the S-O-X holds its gap and 250-day average, the semiconductor rebound remains intact.

26
00:02:48,983 --> 00:02:55,956
For the VIX, holding below 18 favors bulls, while breaking 22 signals a secondary retest.

27
00:02:55,956 --> 00:03:02,206
Inside the tech sector, capital rotated violently out of software and into AI hardware.

28
00:03:02,206 --> 00:03:07,844
Optical networking, memory chips, and NeoCloud infrastructure led the market higher.

29
00:03:07,844 --> 00:03:14,682
CoreWeave ignited the reversal, posting 170 percent revenue growth and raising full-year guidance.

30
00:03:14,682 --> 00:03:20,454
The cloud provider holds 9 billion dollars in binding customer prepayments over the next quarter.

31
00:03:20,454 --> 00:03:27,648
Management pledged no new unsecured debt at current yields, projecting full-year profitability by 2028.

32
00:03:27,648 --> 00:03:34,461
While heavy capital intensity remains a long-term risk, CoreWeave crushed the immediate credit-bubble narrative.

33
00:03:34,461 --> 00:03:42,059
Across the Pacific, South Korea's KOSPI index surged 5 percent, triggering two straight upward circuit breakers.

34
00:03:42,059 --> 00:03:48,505
Leveraged retail traders piled into Samsung and SK Hynix, which command half the index.

35
00:03:48,505 --> 00:03:55,295
While consumer memory gains remain modest, data center High Bandwidth Memory faces severe shortages.

36
00:03:55,424 --> 00:04:01,611
Wall Street's primary motive for pumping AI hardware is next week's massive Anthropic IPO.

37
00:04:01,561 --> 00:04:08,093
Anthropic will price on November 18 and debut November 19 on Nasdaq under ticker A-N-T.

38
00:04:08,093 --> 00:04:14,600
The company is offering 825 million shares between 70 and 78 dollars per share.

39
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:22,002
Combined with 26 billion dollars from tech giants, total financing reaches 90.4 billion dollars.

40
00:04:22,002 --> 00:04:28,559
Its 1.4 trillion dollar valuation reflects a 30 percent discount from last month's private mark.

41
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:34,944
That places Anthropic twelfth in the S and P 500, right between Tesla and Eli Lilly.

42
00:04:34,944 --> 00:04:41,488
Underwriters Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley hold a 15 percent greenshoe option to stabilize trading.

43
00:04:41,488 --> 00:04:50,029
Third-quarter revenue reached 17 billion dollars, surging 45-fold over six quarters across 12,000 enterprise clients.

44
00:04:50,029 --> 00:04:55,936
Yet a 30 percent debut pop would push valuation to a lofty 22 times sales.

45
00:04:55,936 --> 00:05:02,811
Anthropic also carries 900 billion dollars in rigid multi-year compute leases across 30 gigawatts.

46
00:05:02,811 --> 00:05:09,478
Furthermore, common shares carry zero voting rights, leaving seven founders in absolute control.

47
00:05:09,478 --> 00:05:15,850
Paradoxically, major Anthropic shareholders Amazon and Google saw mixed stock reactions.

48
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:23,105
Amazon's 18 billion dollar stake is up 14-fold, and Google's 33 billion quadrupled on paper.

49
00:05:23,105 --> 00:05:31,316
However, paper gains cannot offset Amazon's 220 billion dollar 2026 Capex and negative free cash flow.

50
00:05:31,316 --> 00:05:37,468
The more compute Anthropic demands, the more cash Amazon burns building data centers today.

51
00:05:37,468 --> 00:05:43,914
Meanwhile, Anthropic launched Claude Sheets and meeting tools, while OpenAI entered online travel.

52
00:05:43,914 --> 00:05:52,027
Institutions dumped Expedia, Booking, Airbnb, and Microsoft, using software stocks to fund hardware buys.

53
00:05:52,027 --> 00:05:57,370
In individual equities, four high-conviction buy and sell signals stand out today.

54
00:05:57,370 --> 00:06:03,375
Nvidia, ticker N-V-D-A, flashes a tactical sell signal on intraday bounces.

55
00:06:03,375 --> 00:06:09,282
Nvidia stalled at its 5-day moving average yesterday before plunging in after-hours trading.

56
00:06:09,282 --> 00:06:15,164
The New York Times reported CEO Jensen Huang had an affair with executive Kimberly Powell.

57
00:06:15,164 --> 00:06:23,252
Leadership instability compounds risks ahead of next week's earnings, congressional hearings, and grey-market export crackdowns.

58
00:06:23,252 --> 00:06:30,973
Sell Nvidia at its 5-day moving average resistance and cut leveraged tech calls near Q-Q-Q 700 dollars.

59
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:38,032
Rotate that capital into Advanced Micro Devices, ticker A-M-D, which flashes an actionable buy signal.

60
00:06:38,032 --> 00:06:44,135
Hyperscalers are actively adding A-M-D Instinct accelerators to prevent single-vendor lock-in.

61
00:06:44,135 --> 00:06:50,642
Furthermore, CEO Lisa Su offers superior management stability without governance overhang.

62
00:06:50,642 --> 00:06:58,436
Accumulate A-M-D on intraday dips while Intel, ticker I-N-T-C, captures secondary enterprise inference demand.

63
00:06:58,436 --> 00:07:04,968
Micron Technology, ticker M-U, also flashes a strong buy signal on technical pullbacks.

64
00:07:04,968 --> 00:07:12,407
Micron surged 12 percent yesterday after successfully defending its 250-day moving average support last week.

65
00:07:12,407 --> 00:07:18,608
With High Bandwidth Memory sold out, Micron's upcycle carries a two-year fundamental runway.

66
00:07:18,608 --> 00:07:25,777
Buy Micron on retracements toward its 250-day moving average, using a break below as your stop-loss.

67
00:07:25,777 --> 00:07:33,105
Nebius, ticker N-B-I-S, offers a tactical buy targeting its 250-day average on tonight's earnings.

68
00:07:33,105 --> 00:07:40,042
Conversely, Microsoft, ticker M-S-F-T, triggers a tactical sell and trim signal on rallies.

69
00:07:40,042 --> 00:07:48,056
Microsoft 365 generates nearly one-third of company revenue, now directly targeted by Anthropic's Claude Sheets.

70
00:07:48,056 --> 00:07:54,686
While enterprise switching costs remain high, institutions are using Microsoft as a liquidity source.

71
00:07:54,686 --> 00:08:01,488
Trim Microsoft positions today and avoid chasing Anthropic above 78 dollars in secondary trading.

72
00:08:01,488 --> 00:08:05,495
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

73
00:08:05,495 --> 00:08:09,662
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
